  "observations": [
    "QN90A first refused occupied on-demand staging. Known service archives were subsequently preserved by a journaled directory rename and restored byte-for-byte.",
    "QN90A refused to map the library from writable staging. The trusted managed loader now establishes a private read-only code bind before loading C; no platform policy or file capabilities change.",
    "An initial owner GID assumption was refused. Both supported TVs were observed to use owner UID 5001 and GID 100; the native contract and fixtures now pin those fields.",
    "An initial staged script argument was refused by Samsung shell policy. Native execution now reads verified bounded bytes and uses the same sh -c contract as the managed runner.",
    "Earlier incomplete QN90A rounds are retained as separate failure evidence; their cleanup and baseline restoration were verified. No failed operation was silently retried or converted into managed execution.",
    "S90D synchronous timer stopping timed out after the .NET fallback timer had already been disarmed. Read-only inspection proved both native services completed and SDK remained on loopback; remaining owned timers were stopped without blocking, and final state was verified without replaying acquisition."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Managed NativeEntry and Samsung trusted dotnet/runtime remain required for capability entry and the read-only code mount. This is not .NET-free acquisition.",
    "Explicit opt-in root.execute(native_bundle=...) only; default setup, allowlisted app cleanup, service acquisition and held managed bootstrap remain unchanged.",
    "No firmware expansion, PID-1 namespace cache mutations, optional-app cleanup, reboot, standby, native-default selection, or persistent capability changes.",
    "Commands must remain within bounded supervision; deliberately detached work requires separately journaled service mechanisms.",
    "Private source/build manifests, device identities, raw commands and receipts remain outside Git."
  ]
